  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Was testing the new graph system and came across a couple of quite annoying bugs / usability issues:\n- Clicking \"open graph\" will always reopen the graph window on the same \"window group\" as the Scene window. So if you have a vertical split with Scene on the top and Udon on the bottom - clicking \"Open Graph\" either in the welcome section or in the UdonBehaviour component will jump the graph to the top stack, so you can't see both Scene and Udon canvas at the same time anymore.\n- Noodle Drop Search seems to always appear in the top portion of the screen, as if the graph window is there. If you press enter on any node - the node will be created at the position of the search popup (so it can be beyond the edge of visible graph canvas and you'll have to go up and then bring it back down)\n- The udon watermark is absolutely gigantic to the point of being a bit distracting\n- The grid in the default theme is very contrasty and interferes with the content of the graph adding a lot of visual noise\n- variable settings are gigantic\n- node titles are also gigantic which makes it harder to fit a lot of nodes into the canvas while keeping the properties visible (zooming helps ofc, but this feels a bit unnecessary)\nGreat job on the updated graphs, though. This feels much better!",
